# Implementation Plan - SQL Restoration Stabilization

The "Restoration Failed" error you encountered is a `Broken Pipe` issue. This happened because the database client (`psql`) was configured to run a setup command and then immediately exit, while our system was still trying to stream your 114MB file into it.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Environment Variables:** I will switch to using `PGOPTIONS` to set the `staging` schema. This is the industrial standard for configuring `psql` sessions that read from a stream.

## Proposed Changes

---

### [Component] Restoration Service
#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- **Fix `psql` Arguments**: Remove the `-c "SET search_path TO staging;"` flag which was causing the premature exit.
- **Use Environment Configuration**: Pass `search_path=staging` via the `PGOPTIONS` environment variable when starting the restoration process.
- **Improved Error Diagnostics**: Update the streaming loop to catch `BrokenPipeError`. Instead of just failing, it will now capture and log the specific reason the database rejected the stream (e.g., a constraint violation or syntax error in the dump).

